input.findings:
## Root cause

A dimension name may legitimately be the empty string `''` (e.g. `dataset.dimensions: ['x', '']`). `createDimensions` preserves it: `src/data/helper/createDimensions.ts:143` guards with `userDimName != null` and `src/data/helper/createDimensions.ts:275` with `resultItem.name == null`, so `''` survives as a real dimension name, and `SeriesData.mapDimension('y')` returns `''`. Several places then test that name for *truthiness* instead of `!= null`, so `''` is treated as "no dimension".

I reproduced this with a scratch jest spec (deleted afterwards, tree left clean):

* `dataset: {dimensions: ['x', ''], source: [['a',1],['b',2],['c',3]]}` + `series: [{type:'line', areaStyle:{}}]`
  → `data.mapDimension('y') === ''`, and the resulting `ECPolygon.shape.stackedOnPoints` is `[]` while `shape.points` is `[137.5,235, 262.5,150, 387.5,65]`. The area baseline is missing entirely (`ECPolygon.buildPath` at `src/chart/line/poly.ts:400-405` calls `drawSegment(ctx, stackedOnPoints, ...)` over an empty array, so the polygon is never closed).
* After a second `setOption` (animated update path) it gets worse: `lineAnimationDiff` reads `oldStackedOnPoints[oldIdx2]` from that empty array (`src/chart/line/lineAnimationDiff.ts:110-111`), so the whole `stackedOnPoints` buffer becomes `NaN, NaN, ...`.
* With `stack: 'total'`, the two stacked series render *identically* (no stacking at all) because `isDimensionStacked(data, '')` returns `false`, and `dataStack` skips the series so `stackResultDimension` is never computed.
* When it is the *category/base* dimension that is named `''` (`dimensions: ['', 'v']` + `stack`), `stackedByDimension === ''`; once `dataStack`'s guard is fixed, `SeriesData.rawIndexOf('')` throws `Error: Do not supported yet` in `__DEV__` builds — this is the hard "render error".

All four sites below must change together; fixing only some of them either leaves stacking silently broken or converts the silent breakage into a thrown error.

---

### 1. `src/chart/line/LineView.ts:130-148` — primary fix (the areaStyle bug)

Current (lines 130-148):

```ts
function getStackedOnPoints(
    coordSys: Cartesian2D | Polar,
    data: SeriesData,
    dataCoordInfo: ReturnType<typeof prepareDataCoordInfo>
) {
    if (!dataCoordInfo.valueDim) {
        return [];
    }
```

Replace line 135 only:

```ts
    if (dataCoordInfo.valueDim == null) {
```

`dataCoordInfo.valueDim` comes from `src/chart/line/helper.ts:51` (`const valueDim = data.mapDimension(valueAxisDim);`) and is typed `valueDim: string` in the `CoordInfo` interface at `src/chart/line/helper.ts:34`. No type change needed. Note `getStackedOnPoints` never actually *uses* `valueDim` — it is purely a "does this series have a value dimension" guard, which is why the empty-string false negative silently produced a length-0 array.

This single change fixes both the first-render broken area and the `NaN` corruption in `src/chart/line/lineAnimationDiff.ts`.

### 2. `src/data/helper/dataStackHelper.ts:205-209` — stacking detection

Current:

```ts
export function isDimensionStacked(data: SeriesData, stackedDim: string): boolean {
    // Each single series only maps to one pair of axis. So we do not need to
    // check stackByDim, whatever stacked by a dimension or stacked by index.
    return !!stackedDim && stackedDim === data.getCalculationInfo('stackedDimension');
}
```

Replace line 208 with:

```ts
    return stackedDim != null && stackedDim === data.getCalculationInfo('stackedDimension');
}
```

The `stackedDim != null` guard must be kept (not dropped): callers pass `dims[1]`, which is `undefined` for 1-dimension coord systems, and `getCalculationInfo('stackedDimension')` is `undefined` for non-stacked data, so a bare `===` would report `undefined === undefined` as "stacked".

`stackedDimension` itself is produced at `src/data/helper/dataStackHelper.ts:191` (`stackedDimension: stackedDimInfo && stackedDimInfo.name`) — that expression already yields `''` for an empty name and `undefined` when there is no stack dim, so it needs no change.

Call sites that depend on this and are fixed transitively (verify, no edits needed): `src/layout/points.ts:51,54`, `src/chart/line/helper.ts:61,65`, `src/layout/barGrid.ts:489`, `src/layout/barPolar.ts:104`, `src/component/marker/markerHelper.ts:65`, `src/data/helper/dataStackHelper.ts:212` (`getStackedDimension`, used by `src/coord/axisHelper.ts:338` and `src/component/marker/MarkLineView.ts:97`).

### 3. `src/processor/dataStack.ts:65-70` — stack values never computed

Current (lines 65-70):

```ts
            // If stacked on axis that do not support data stack.
            if (!stackInfo.stackedDimension
                || !(stackInfo.isStackedByIndex || stackInfo.stackedByDimension)
            ) {
                return;
            }
```

Replace with:

```ts
            // If stacked on axis that do not support data stack.
            if (stackInfo.stackedDimension == null
                || !(stackInfo.isStackedByIndex || stackInfo.stackedByDimension != null)
            ) {
                return;
            }
```

Without this, a series whose value dim (or whose stack-by dim) is named `''` is dropped from the stack group, so `stackResultDimension` stays 0/NaN and every stacked line collapses onto the axis baseline (I observed all points at y=320 for a 400px chart).

Do NOT touch `src/processor/dataStack.ts:47-49` (`const stack = seriesModel.get('stack'); if (stack) {`) or `src/data/helper/dataStackHelper.ts:91` (`const mayStack = !!(seriesModel && seriesModel.get('stack'));`) — those are truthiness checks on the `stack` *option*, where `''` intentionally means "do not stack" (documented by the adjacent comments).

### 4. `src/data/SeriesData.ts:867-879` — throws once #3 is fixed (required in sync)

Current:

```ts
    rawIndexOf(dim: SeriesDimensionName, value: OrdinalNumber): number {
        const invertedIndices = dim && this._invertedIndicesMap[dim];
        if (__DEV__) {
            if (!invertedIndices) {
                throw new Error('Do not supported yet');
            }
        }
```

Replace line 868 with:

```ts
        const invertedIndices = dim != null && this._invertedIndicesMap[dim];
```

`dim && ...` short-circuits to `''` when the stack-by dimension is named `''`, so `!invertedIndices` is true and `__DEV__` builds throw `Do not supported yet` from `src/processor/dataStack.ts:140` (`stackInfo.data.rawIndexOf(stackInfo.stackedByDimension, byValue)`). Keeping the `dim != null &&` form preserves the existing `undefined` → throw behaviour. Verified: with #3 alone the test throws; with #3 + #4 the two stacked series get correct, distinct `points`/`stackedOnPoints`.

---

## Verification I ran

Applied all four edits, then reverted them (`git checkout -- src/`; `git status` shows no `src/` changes now).

* Non-stacked, `dimensions: ['x','']`: `stackedOnPoints` became `[137.5,320, 262.5,320, 387.5,320]` (correct baseline) instead of `[]`.
* Animated update path: `stackedOnPoints` became real numbers instead of all `NaN`.
* Stacked, `dimensions: ['x','']`: series 0 `points [137.5,277.5, 262.5,235, 387.5,192.5]` / `stackedOn [...,320,...]`; series 1 `points [137.5,235, 262.5,150, 387.5,65]` / `stackedOn` = series 0's points — correctly stacked.
* Stacked with empty *base* dim (`dimensions: ['','v']`): no throw, correct stacking.
* Full unit suite green: `npx jest --config test/ut/jest.config.cjs --coverage=false` → 23 suites / 184 tests passed.

## Tests

No existing spec under `test/ut/spec` covers line `areaStyle` or `stackedOnPoints` (`rg areaStyle test/ut` → no hits; the closest related specs are `test/ut/spec/data/SeriesData.test.ts` and `test/ut/spec/data/createDimensions.test.ts`, neither of which exercises empty dimension names).

`test/ut/jest.config.cjs:49` already includes `'**/spec/chart/**/*.test.ts'` in `testMatch`, but `test/ut/spec/chart/` does not exist yet. A new spec at `test/ut/spec/chart/line/LineView.test.ts` will be picked up automatically. Suggested assertions, using `createChart` from `test/ut/core/utHelper.ts` and reaching the view via `(chart as any)._chartsMap[seriesModel.__viewId]._polygon.shape`:

1. `dimensions: ['x', '']` + `series: [{type:'line', areaStyle:{}}]` → `polygon.shape.stackedOnPoints.length === polygon.shape.points.length`, and every value finite.
2. Same option, then a second `setOption` with different/longer source → `stackedOnPoints` contains no `NaN`.
3. `dimensions: ['x', '']` + two `stack: 'total'` line series → series 1's `points` differ from series 0's, and series 1's `stackedOnPoints` equal series 0's `points`.
4. `dimensions: ['', 'v']` + two `stack: 'total'` series → `setOption` does not throw (guards the `rawIndexOf` regression).

Manual/visual test pages that exercise these code paths: `test/area-stack.html`, `test/area-origin.html`, `test/areaLineUpdate.html`, `test/line-step.html`.
